  *Correct.*  The line indeed has slope \(2\) and covers the missing point.

- **\(k=3\).**  “Use the \(n-3\) vertical lines \(x=1,\dots ,x=n-3\).  The uncovered set is \(T_3\).  The three sunny lines … contain respectively the points … which are exactly the six points of \(T_3\).”  

  *Issue (Justification Gap).*  
